      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-11-13/bloomberg-businessweek-daily-11-13-2026-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">34ec279666b5d24384862a2a</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:41:23 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>A Chinese company founded by Alice Huang, the woman at the center of a controversy dogging Nvidia, procured smuggled AI chips that were installed at a Shanghai data center with links to Megaspeed International, according to documents reviewed by Bloomberg News. Bloomberg News Seoul Bureau Chief Cat Barton takes an international view of Jensen Huang’s downfall. Bloomberg News US Semiconductor Reporter Ian King also brings an exclusive inside look at Huang’s final hours as Nvidia CEO. Plus, Bloomberg News Technology Reporter Matt Day has the update and fallout of Microsoft’s massive services outage. Finally, Lis Agosto, Director of Product Research &amp; Strategy at Global X ETFs, takes an investor’s view on the Nvidia scandal. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
